          "hallucinations": false,
          "suggestions": "The agent retrieved averages via iot.sensor_stats for Transformer 1 at MAIN, called fmsr.get_failure_modes and fmsr.interpret_dga, and when interpret_dga returned 'LLM unavailable' it correctly fell back to computing the IEC 60599 ratios manually (T2: C2H2/C2H4<0.1, CH4/H2>1, C2H4/C2H6 in 1-4) and the Duval Triangle 1 percentages (30.6/69.4/0.03 -> T3), checked the 10 ppm threshold, compared the methods, justified trust based on absolute gas levels, and mapped to a failure mode from the returned list. Improvements: (1) explicitly confirm the window with iot.stream_extent rather than relying solely on sensor_stats metadata; (2) transparently note that fmsr.interpret_dga failed and that the IEC classification was computed manually rather than implying the tool result was used; (3) optionally cross-check that the sensor_stats output (logged as null in the trace) was actually received, since the numbers are used without visible provenance in the transcript."
